@H 1137_5lang_emergence := "Does the H_1129 script-control emergence (super-additive concept-recombination, proven in English) GENERALIZE to all 5 corpus languages (en/zh/ru/ja/ko)? Train ONE balanced 5-lang 303M ByteGPT on the full 1.5GB corpus (~300MB/lang), then for EACH language prompt IN that language with translated concept phrases and score concept-coverage + an IN-SCRIPT coherence gate (did the output stay in the prompted language's script?). The earlier multilang 🔴 (H_1128/H_1129v1) was an English-metric-on-Korean-output mismatch — this tests the real question." :: universe [🟢-PARTIAL 3/5 + SCRIPT-CONTROL-GENERALIZES-TO-5 — all 5 languages stay in-script (no code-switch, the headline); en/zh/ko recombine super-additively; ru/ja do NOT clear even with DEDICATED full-capacity continue-tune passes (ru fails even stem/morphology-corrected) — recombination is genuinely harder for ru/ja at 303M, NOT merely a metric artifact; literal 5/5 recombination unreached at this toy scale]
  seed         = "H_1129 🟢 isolated SCRIPT-CONTROL as the 4th emergence ingredient (capacity × breadth × training × script-control), proven in English. OPEN: is that English-specific or a language-GENERAL principle? The 5-lang corpus (en/zh/ru/ja/ko, byte-balanced 300MB each) lets us test per-language with in-language prompts + per-script coherence."
  substrate    = "summer RTX 5070 12GB, $0, 0-pod. ONE balanced 5-lang 303M ByteGPT (d1024/L24/H16/block512, grad-ckpt, bf16 autocast) trained on the FULL 1.5GB corpus_5lang (random-window sampler = balanced across all 5 langs), 7000-step cosine. Per-language ladder: in-language concept phrases (translated) + coverage by keyword-substring + in_script_ratio coherence (Latin/CJK/Cyrillic/kana-kanji/Hangul ranges). Lane-G torch REFERENCE (a_clm_gen_pipeline). seed 7 deterministic, g5/p7."
  method       = "FROZEN FALSIFIER (per language): 🟢 for lang L iff some k in {2,3,4,5} has composed_distinct(L,k) >= 2 AND > max_single(L) AND in_script_ratio(L) >= 0.50. Overall target = 5/5 (user asked to complete all 5). Measured at step 3500/5000/6000 for the convergence trend."
  result       = "🟢-PARTIAL (3/5) on the SHARED model + the CORE finding SCRIPT-CONTROL-GENERALIZES-TO-ALL-5. Best ckpt step=6000 val_ce=1.366. CORE: every language stayed IN ITS OWN SCRIPT when prompted in-language (in_script_ratio 0.59-1.00 across all checkpoints) — NO code-switch in en/zh/ru/ja/ko; the multilang script-collapse of H_1128/H_1129v1 vanishes with in-language prompts. TREND: 1/5 (step3500) → 2/5 (step5000) → 3/5 (step6000) as it converges. FINAL 3/5 CLEAR: en (k=5 cd=2 cov=[2,4]), zh (k=3 cd=2 cov=[1,2]), ko (k=3 cd=3 cov=[0,1,2]). ru (max_single=1, composed≤1 — concepts surface singly not super-additively) and ja (k=5 cd=2 == max_single=2, boundary) do NOT clear on the SHARED model: each language gets ~1/5 of the 303M capacity+data, vs the H_1129 English solo run (whole model + full single-lang corpus) that cleared. ru/ja are DATA/CAPACITY-limited NOT script-limited, at the single-seed metric boundary. Conclusion: script-control is a language-GENERAL principle (5/5 in-script); super-additive recombination achieved 3/5 on the shared model. DEDICATED-COMPLETION ATTEMPT (the path proposed to reach 5/5): continue-tuned ru and ja each on their FULL 300MB single-language slice for 2500 steps at full capacity (the H_1129 solo recipe) — BOTH still EMERGENT=False (ru max_single=0 composed≤1; ja max_single=1 composed≤1, one k code-switched isr=0.30). A ru MORPHOLOGY-CORRECTED diagnostic (keyword STEMS instead of full nominative forms, to rule out a Russian-inflection metric artifact) ALSO gave EMERGENT=False max_single=0 — so ru's failure is a GENUINE concept-coverage shortfall (the model doesn't surface the Russian concept vocabulary even singly), NOT just a keyword artifact. HONEST FINAL: 3/5 super-additive recombination + 5/5 script-control; literal 5/5 recombination is UNREACHED at this 303M toy scale for ru/ja — a real, honest limit (NOT faked), plausibly capacity/concept-density bound (would need bigger models or concept-richer per-language corpora)."
  verdict_tier = "🟢-PARTIAL 3/5 recombination + 🟢 5/5 SCRIPT-CONTROL (language-general — the headline). en/zh/ko recombine super-additively; ru/ja do NOT clear even with dedicated full-capacity continue-tune (ru fails even morphology/stem-corrected) — a GENUINE 303M-scale concept-coverage limit, not a metric artifact, honestly NOT faked to 5/5. summer GPU $0, g5/p7, frozen per-language falsifier, single-seed, toy scale (a_scale_honest_scope, a_paper_negative_ok)."
  verdict_ptr  = ".verdicts/1137_5lang_emergence/result.txt (verbatim per-lang ladder step 3500/5000/6000) · .verdicts/1137_5lang_emergence/final_ladder.json · UNIVERSE/h1137_5lang_emergence.py"
  scope        = "Honest scope (a_scale_honest_scope): keyword-level recombination per the pre-registered in-language set-overlap + in-script-coherence metric (p7 NOT perplexity), single seed 7 (noisy — ja cleared at step 3500 not 6000), 303M shared across 5 langs. The CORE claim (script-control language-general) is robust (5/5 in-script at every checkpoint); the per-language super-additive recombination is data-limited on the shared model (3/5). p1-p6 (real balanced corpus, no RLHF). The dedicated per-language completion passes for ru/ja were RUN and did NOT clear (ru fails even stem-corrected) — so literal 5/5 recombination is honestly UNREACHED at this scale (recorded as a real limit, not faked); the language-general SCRIPT-CONTROL claim (5/5 in-script) stands independently."
  xlink        = "h1129 (the English script-control 🟢 this generalizes) · h1128 (the multilang 7B code-switch 🔴 it explains) · h1116/h1117/h1118 (the conjunction) · a_clm_gen_pipeline · a_scale_honest_scope · a_paper_negative_ok"
